sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 8, docs/reference/development-containers.md#migrate-a-checkout-instance): one checkout Instance moves into a container, with its code and its database. A default Instance moves before the other Instances of its Project, and keeps its checkout until its last worktree has moved. The command exists only until the last checkout Instance has moved.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:migrate
  %% kind: instance.migrate
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as New container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:migrate<br/>INSTANCE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:migrate INSTANCE`
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve runtime<br/>address · T3 port
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the Instance is an active checkout Instance on an `app-dev` Node
  %%> - a non-default Instance needs its Project's default Instance in a container first, else `instance.default_not_migrated`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the runtime record is reserved; the checkout stays the Instance's runtime until the run succeeds
  %%> - a repository read token goes to the vault
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-migrate
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  SW->>N: Stop the Instance<br/>Ansible · tags quiesce
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops the Processes and puts the Route on the wake page, so nothing writes the checkout or the database while they move
  SW->>N: Launch, build repository<br/>Ansible · tags container
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - launches a container from the image with the bridge address, limits and idmapped mounts
  %%> - fetches the Instance's branches on the Node with the read token and pushes them into a standalone repository in `/srv/workspace`; a non-default checkout is a worktree, so its `.git` is never copied
  %%> - copies the checkout's uncommitted and ignored files into the workspace, and sets the owners, group and ACLs
  SW->>N: Clone the database<br/>child database-clone
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the database family clones the checkout's database into a new one: a template copy on the same server, a dump and restore across servers
  %%> - the old database stays until the run succeeds
  SW->>C: Start the container<br/>.env · T3 · Processes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes `.env` with the new database, keeping the Instance's `APP_KEY`, and starts the Processes as `orbit`
  %%> - a non-default Instance also gets `/etc/orbit/instance`, the agent settings and its T3 server, registered as in create
  %%> - a default Instance gets its first `seed-<commit>` snapshot
  SW->>N: Move the Route<br/>child route-update
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - points the Instance's Route at FrankenPHP in the container, and withdraws the checkout's PHP-FPM pool
  alt all steps pass
    SW->>N: Remove the checkout<br/>checkout · old database
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the checkout and the old database; a default's checkout stays until its last worktree has moved
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record container runtime
  else a step fails
    SW->>N: Restore the checkout<br/>Processes · Route
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the checkout and its database are untouched, so the Instance serves as before; the new container and database are removed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
